    description: "Prior-tranche flags from WI-vafad (tranche 1 / tranche 2), never filed, re-verified ACCEPT at dev fe3c32259d (docs/audits/0022, prior-backlog section). INV-nular's swept family \"lifecycle callbacks and close calls declared as transfers\" (F4, PR #606: Network.Socket.close removed, \"a FIN is not a payload any line of the program produced\") turns up again in two languages the 08-28 sweep did not reach:\n\n  python  asyncio.StreamWriter.close  net_send -> NONE   `return self._transport.close()` (streams.py:357-358). The selector transport's close only marks the transport closing and schedules connection_lost (selector_events.py:867-875), and flushes nothing itself.\n  go      net/smtp.Client.Close       net_send -> NONE   c.Text.Close() -> c.conn.Close() (smtp.go:77-78). It sends no SMTP payload; QUIT is Client.Quit (:415-421).\n\nnet_send is a SINK, so each row today accepts a tainted value as \"sent\" at a call that transmits nothing the program produced. Egress stays represented: asyncio StreamWriter.write / drain, go smtp NewClient / Dial / SendMail / Mail / Rcpt / Data (go.yaml:292-296).\n\nFIX OBLIGATION: removing a net_send row removes a sink. ADR-0049 ruling 3 per language: both arms cold, read every moved verdict back, never pin a removal."  # 1259
